<%# locals: (message:, owner:, body: nil, landing: false) %>
<%#
  One message of a thread: who, when, and the body, stacked newest last
  (ruling D3 of .scratch/messaging-rework/PRD.md). A row the owner has not read
  is tinted and chipped "New" -- the warning vocabulary every unread mark uses.
  `owner` is a local rather than the message_owner helper so a broadcast render
  (a live reply, slice 5) needs no controller.

  `body` is the body as _thread draws it, a search's matches marked; a card
  rendered on its own -- a live reply, a read-state morph -- draws it plain.
  `landing` makes this the card a search's hit opens on, or the stepper last
  stepped to: data-landing, which rings it. Scrolled to the top of the pane or
  the page, it stops clear of the stepper pinned there (_messages_panel):
  72px down: the pane's 16px padding, the stepper's 8px inset and 36px
  height, and a 12px gap -- 16px on the page, whose padding is 12px.
  review_pane_controller keeps the body (data-message-body; a body never
  changes once sent) and data-landing through a morph, so the card's own
  renders, which know no search, never take them away.
%>
<% unread = message.unread?(owner.id) %>
<%# data-unread is how thread_live_controller knows a live card is someone else's, still unread. %>
<article id="<%= dom_id(message, :card) %>"
         class="<%= class_names("rounded-lg border border-line p-3 mb-3",
                                "data-landing:ring-2 data-landing:ring-primary data-landing:scroll-mt-18 data-landing:scroll-mb-4", "bg-warning/10": unread) %>"
         <%= tag.attributes(data: { unread: (true if unread), landing: (true if landing) }) %>>
  <div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-2 mb-1 text-sm text-stone-subtle">
    <%# A row written as a team names the team; to the team's members alone
        (PersonMessage#reveals_author_to?) it names its author, as an individual
        row would, chipped with the team it was sent or replied as. An
        individual row by someone marked a team member who has since left the
        team says so to everyone (#former_team). %>
    <% revealed = message.reveals_author_to?(owner.id) %>
    <span class="font-semibold text-base text-heading"><%= revealed ? message.author_callsign : message.sender_name %></span>
    <% if revealed %>
      <%= ui_badge "#{message.reply_to_id ? "Replied" : "Sent"} as #{message.sender_name}", :secondary %>
    <% elsif (former = message.former_team) %>
      <%= ui_badge "Former #{former.title} Member", :secondary %>
    <% end %>
    <time datetime="<%= message.created_at.iso8601 %>"><%= datetime_format message.created_at, year: message.sent_prior_year? %></time>
    <%= ui_badge "New", :warning if unread %>
  </div>
  <%# wrap-anywhere: a long URL is one unbreakable word that would push the card past the pane.
      The editor's HTML is sanitized (rich_text) and read with lexxy-content's
      rules; a plain body -- everything from before the editor -- keeps its
      line breaks and has its addresses and numbers linked. %>
  <div class="<%= class_names("text-body wrap-anywhere", "lexxy-content": message.rich_text?) %>" data-message-body><%= body || message_body(message) %></div>
</article>
